extends Control
## OoT-style pause screen (after kaleido_scope, ovl_kaleido_scope in zeldaret/oot).
##
## The pages stand on the sides of a drum around the camera, in OoT's order
## (pause.h) going right: SELECT ITEM, MAP, QUEST STATUS, then the JOURNAL and
## OPTIONS, which OoT does not have, and EQUIPMENT, left of SELECT ITEM as in
## OoT. OoT's box has four sides; with six pages the drum is a hexagon, each
## page still 128 units wide and seen from 128 units away (the eye sits behind
## the center, opposite the active page). Flipping (R = right, Z = left, or pushing the
## cursor past a page edge, KaleidoScope_HandlePageToggles) slides the eye in a
## straight line to the next side over PAGE_SWITCH_NSTEPS = 16 frames, so the
## pages swing past in perspective (KaleidoScope_UpdatePageSwitch). Opening
## swings the drum down from above. The name panel under the pages names
## whatever the cursor is on.
##
## B on any page asks "Would you like to save?" (KaleidoScope_Update's
## PAUSE_STATE_SAVE_PROMPT); YES writes the game to its file (SaveGame).
## OoT then closes the whole pause screen, YES or NO; here (the user's call,
## Beta 1.6.0) either answer goes back to the page you were on.
##
## The cursor moves as OoT's does (Beta 1.6.0): the stick steps at once, then
## after R_PAUSE_STICK_REPEAT_DELAY_FIRST (10 frames) every third frame; on
## SELECT ITEM and EQUIPMENT it skips empty slots; and past a page's edge it
## stops on that side's page-turn button (cursorSpecialPos), where holding the
## stick on for 10 more frames, or pushing it again, turns the page
## (KaleidoScope_HandlePageToggles). Turning a page, by the stick or by
## LT / RT, leaves the cursor on the new page's button on the side it came
## from (KaleidoScope_SetupPageSwitch); pushing back onto the page brings the
## cursor to its first slot on that side.
##
## Each page is drawn flat into its own 256x176 SubViewport, then projected onto
## its side of the box here, split into small cells (with near-plane clipping)
## so the texture stays straight.

enum Phase { CLOSED, OPENING, OPEN, SWITCHING, CLOSING }
enum Page { ITEM, MAP, QUEST, JOURNAL, OPTIONS, EQUIP }

